==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlapən/|lang=de}}
* {{a|standard}} {{IPA|[ˈläp(ə)n]|[ˈläʔm̩]|lang=de}}
* {{a|Northern Germany}} {{IPA|['la̝(ʔ)m̩]|lang=de}}
* {{a|Ripuarian, Swiss}} {{IPA|['lɑp.pən]|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|lappe|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|lappo|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{term|*lappa-|lang=gem-pro}}. The form is remarkable because of the unshifted geminate ''-pp-'' (instead of expected Old High German *''lapfo''). Based on the supposedly invariable nature of the consonant shift, {{term||lappo|lang=goh}} would have to be an originally [[Central German|Central]] and [[Low German]] form (compare {{etyl|osx|de}} {{term|lappo|lang=osx}}). This is, however, quite unlikely since the Old High German word is attested as early as the 9th century, and no variants with ''-pf-'' exist. The form remains thus unexplained.

